  "notes": [
    "The paper/README headline 585 pairs and 88 devices differs from released records: 672 rows across 79 devices; 585 is_valid=true rows cover 74 devices.",
    "is_valid is a boolean completeness flag, not a clinical/legal correctness label. local_export_all.py computes it from non-null patent abstract and device text plus presence of extracted entities and company links.",
    "The 87 is_valid=false records must not be recoded as negative patent-device relations or silently discarded.",
    "kg_linked records the original pipeline result, not independent ground truth.",
    "Every one of the 590 positive training pairs occurs in evaluation_dataset.csv; these files are not disjoint train/test sets.",
    "Export overlap does not demonstrate that the paper cross-validation protocol is invalid; the paper describes cross-validation, but its split IDs are not in this release.",
    "Unlisted sampled pairs receive label=0 in export code, so negatives are not verified invalid relationships.",
    "Released gold table contains no per-link disclosure URL, source date, or train/validation/test assignment.",
    "Recursive repository tree at this commit has no code/hpc_run_all.py although README reproduction commands depend on it; no LICENSE file or split manifest was present.",
    "README displays an MIT badge; GitHub repository license metadata is null and no distinct data license was verified.",
    "50,000-patent released corpus includes all gold patent IDs plus sampled distractors; it is not the full 698,191-patent experiment corpus.",
    "This script audits data availability/schema/overlap only. No retrieval baseline or model result was reproduced."
